WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.380
Sequels are a big business in Hollywood, and
every studio loves a franchise.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.049
Still, sometimes a movie just can't pass that
initial bar of quality that gets a sequel

00:00:10.049 --> 00:00:11.969
greenlit in the first place.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:16.280
Filmmakers might have grand plans for a franchise,
only to have them thwarted before they can

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.230
get started because of lousy reviews and low
box office receipts.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:24.689
Here are some planned sequels that were completely
abandoned.

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:26.140
Superman Returns Again

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:31.429
Bryan Singer's Superman sequel from 2006 was
kind of a bad idea from the start.

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:36.480
It followed up the events of Superman II,
ignored Superman III and IV, and two of its

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.510
major plot points revolved around Superman
super-stalking his former girlfriend, Lois

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.570
Lane, as well as a revelation that her son
was their secret love child.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:49.930
Worst of all, the movie didn't really give
Superman very much to do in terms of actually

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:54.100
fighting bad guys, which, y'know, is one of
the things Superman does best.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.120
Warner Bros. pulled the plug on the possibility
of another Singer-helmed sequel, which screenwriter

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:05.290
Michael Dougherty says might've introduced
Brainiac and more Kryptonians to the screen.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.860
"Identify."

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.240
"Try asking nice."

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.140
"Kryptonian…"

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:14.810
Batman Triumphant

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:20.360
George Clooney's first outing as the Caped
Crusader in 1997's Batman and Robin was not

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.610
supposed to be his last.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:26.230
In fact, Warner Bros. was gearing up to bring
back Clooney and co-stars Chris O'Donnell

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:31.140
and Alicia Silverstone for a sequel titled
Batman Triumphant, which would've been directed

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.380
by Joel Schumacher.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:37.460
However, Batman and Robin was a critical joke,
summoning more laughs than its campy script

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.840
ever intended.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:43.120
Audiences who'd flocked to watch Val Kilmer
in the batsuit just two years before simply

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.729
didn't show up to see what Uma Thurman's Poison
Ivy and Arnold Schwarzenegger's Mr. Freeze

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:50.720
would be adding to the villainous fold this
go-round.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.270
Spoiler alert: They didn't miss much — except
for a few terrible puns.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:56.340
"What killed the dinosaurs?

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.020
The ice age!"

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:00.840
"My name is Freeze.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.800
Learn it well for it's the chilling sound
of your doom."

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:07.800
Good times.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.080
If Batman Triumphant had happened as planned,
it reportedly would've relied on the Scarecrow

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.909
and Harley Quinn as the Joker's daughter to
play the bad guys.

00:02:15.909 --> 00:02:20.200
And they would've been joined by fear-gas
induced appearances from the Joker, Penguin,

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.799
Catwoman, Two-Face, and The Riddler in an
effort to get Bruce Wayne committed to Arkham

00:02:24.799 --> 00:02:26.090
Asylum.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.719
Dredd 2

00:02:27.719 --> 00:02:31.599
This is probably the most tragic entry on
the list, since the first Dredd, starring

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:34.459
Karl Urban, is a legitimately amazing movie.

00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:39.739
Unfortunately, it seems that the stink of
Sylvester Stallone's 1995 Judge Dredd adaptation

00:02:39.739 --> 00:02:44.480
was too strong for moviegoers to ignore, and
Dredd failed to find an audience during its

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.709
theatrical run.

00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:49.680
It's a cult hit, though, so there's still
an outside chance Dredd 2 could happen before

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.260
we all get old and die.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:56.879
In fact, in early 2017, producer Adi Shankar
vowed to make some sort of follow-up happen

00:02:56.879 --> 00:02:58.549
— even if it's animated.

00:02:58.549 --> 00:03:02.019
He told Collider, "I'm gonna make it happen
at some point.

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:05.310
It may not be live-action, but it's going
to happen at some point.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.189
There will be more Judge Dredd at some point."

00:03:08.189 --> 00:03:10.269
Fantastic Four 3

00:03:10.269 --> 00:03:14.799
The first cinematic outing from 20th Century
Fox's adaptation of Marvel's first family

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:19.749
wasn't great — but it did well enough to
spawn a sequel, 2007's Rise of the Silver

00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:20.749
Surfer.

00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:24.919
This one was actually a bit better, featuring
a version of Galactus and the Power Cosmic.

00:03:24.919 --> 00:03:27.549
But it still wasn't good enough by a long
shot.

00:03:27.549 --> 00:03:32.060
The franchise ground to a screeching halt
after it underperformed at the box office,

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.930
and as star Chris Evans later told MTV, no
one from the cast ever even got a call from

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.059
Fox about coming back for more.

00:03:39.059 --> 00:03:43.909
Just goes to show you that signing a three-picture
deal doesn't mean as much as you might hope.

00:03:43.909 --> 00:03:48.389
"Oh my God, come on!"

00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:50.000
Green Lantern 2

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.239
The original 2011 Ryan Reynolds vehicle was
supposed to kickstart a whole DC superhero

00:03:55.239 --> 00:03:59.290
franchise to rival Marvel's ever-expanding
cinematic universe.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:04.749
DC's corporate parent, Warner Bros., bet big
on Green Lantern, spending a whopping $200

00:04:04.749 --> 00:04:08.379
million on the movie — and it only barely
turned a profit.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:12.339
Between the film's cliffhangers and its efforts
to build a big world for Green Lantern to

00:04:12.339 --> 00:04:16.889
play in, the movie was considered a failure,
and all plans for a sequel were scrapped.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:22.120
Now Green Lantern's set to be rebooted to
fit in with the DC Extended Universe…presumably,

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:25.080
at least the studio hopes, for the final time.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.419
The Mortal Instruments: City of Ashes

00:04:27.419 --> 00:04:32.729
By all estimations, the adaptation of Cassandra
Clare's Young Adult sensation series The Mortal

00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:37.180
Instruments seemed like it'd be the next big
hit in the vein of Twilight and The Hunger

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:38.180
Games.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:42.180
It had all the essential ingredients, including
a huge book-loving fanbase that clung to every

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.680
moment of the production phase and cast members
who engaged in an offscreen romance to mirror

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.120
their screen counterparts.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:53.669
So, naturally, 2013's The Mortal Instruments:
City of Bones was expected to launch an entire

00:04:53.669 --> 00:04:57.930
franchise that would've capitalized on the
craze surrounding its sister series.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:02.169
The script for City of Ashes had already been
drawn up, and the actors and crew already

00:05:02.169 --> 00:05:06.169
had a production schedule in place before
the results of the first film's release came

00:05:06.169 --> 00:05:09.180
through — and put the brakes on everything.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:13.949
It wasn't the early critical blasts that stymied
the sequel — don't forget, scathing reviewers

00:05:13.949 --> 00:05:15.660
stung the Twilight Saga, too.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:20.520
It was the fact that the much-hyped film grossly
disappointed at the box office, making just

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:25.950
half of its production budget back in domestic
sales, and, according to Cassandra Clare herself,

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:30.840
the sequel to Ashes would've been "unrecognizable"
to the book series faithful, thus weakening

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:32.700
audience interest even further.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.720
Ultimately, despite some early signs that
the second Mortal Instruments pic might be

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.140
retooled and eventually made, the project
was abandoned, and the series was instead

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.659
relegated to the small screen by way of Freeform's
Shadowhunters.

00:05:44.659 --> 00:05:47.509
So, it wasn't a total wash.

00:05:47.509 --> 00:05:49.330
Twins 2: Triplets

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:54.009
Twins was something of a high-concept comedy
that revolves entirely around a single sight

00:05:54.009 --> 00:05:59.219
gag: muscle-laden Austrian superman Arnold
Schwarzenegger and teeny tiny Brooklynite

00:05:59.219 --> 00:06:02.509
Danny DeVito play long-lost twins.

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:07.289
The 1988 hit, directed by Ghostbusters mastermind
Ivan Reitman, was a breezy romp in which the

00:06:07.289 --> 00:06:11.509
two stars hung out and goofed off under the
auspices of their characters getting to know

00:06:11.509 --> 00:06:12.509
each other.

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:13.509
"Who are you?"

00:06:13.509 --> 00:06:14.600
"I'm Vincent's brudda."

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.219
"We're twins."

00:06:17.219 --> 00:06:21.310
And because Twins was such a hit, rumors hit
almost immediately after its release that

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.750
a sequel was coming.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:27.120
In 1989, a representative for Reitman said
that the director was considering making a

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.240
movie called...wait for it...Triplets.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.960
The top candidate to play the third long-lost
multiple didn't look anything like the others,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.259
which was essential of course, and was the
hottest comedy star of the moment: Roseanne

00:06:39.259 --> 00:06:40.259
Barr.

00:06:40.259 --> 00:06:44.720
That movie never got made of course, but in
2012, there was renewed talk of Triplets,

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:47.270
without Barr, but with Eddie Murphy.

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:51.180
But considering how many years have passed
with no more news on that front, Triplets

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.550
is probably not gonna happen.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:57.080
"No, don't start diss!"

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.110
Thanks for watching!

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:05.129
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:05.129 --> 00:07:07.740
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

